WEBVTT

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:19.850
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:19.850
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:19.850
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:44.640
One Hundred Billion Stars, One Hundred Billion Lights

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:44.640
Chapter 2

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:53.270
In March of Space Year 794,
Imperial Year 485...

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:57.500
...in the Battle of Van-Fleet Starzone both sides continued to advance and retreat with no clear victor.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:01.980
Under the orders from Fleet Headquarters,
the Grimmelshausen Fleet...

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.740
...including the small unit under Reinhard's
command, headed toward Planet 4.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:13.300
I've fought against the
rebel troops for 56 years.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:21.150
Speaking from that experience, I suppose the
outcome of the battle won't be decided easily...

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:25.780
...considering how chaotic
the present situation is.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:30.770
As such, we have no choice but to retreat
once, re-establish the order of the fleet...

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:34.020
...and reorganize
a plan of attack.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:38.330
If there's no opportunity to reorganize, then that's the end of it.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:42.860
It took him half a century
to figure out such a truism ?

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:45.150
The Space Fleet is not a sanatorium
for old men with Alzheimer's.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:54.120
The 4th planet of
the Van-Fleet Starzone...

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:57.370
...is a gas-comprised star with
a diameter of 120,000 km...

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:58.870
...but it has
several satellites.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:04.030
The largest of them, the second satellite,
is where we'll land and establish a base.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:09.550
I don't think it serves any strategic purpose
to set up a station in such a remote location.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:14.690
Fleet HQ's intention is clearly to isolate the Grimmmelshausen Fleet away from the front line.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:20.120
On this satellite, which we'll call
Van-Fleet 4-2 as a matter of convenience...

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:23.720
...we'll thaw the ice at the north
pole with nuclear fusion bombs...

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.720
...and cover it with a liquid metal membrane
to avoid complete vaporization of the water.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.470
That's where we'll land.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:30.770
Any questions ?

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.720
What a roundabout strategy.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:37.740
If I were the chief commander I would have brought a totally one-sided victory to the Imperial Fleet...

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:40.290
...that would forever
be recorded in our history.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:45.670
The meeting is dismissed.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:52.160
Commodore Musel.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:53.030
Yes, sir.

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.160
What can I do for you ?

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:08.640
I'd like you to set the
sea route with your fleet.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:10.860
Yes, sir.
Mission acknowledged.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:16.020
But you really
are very young.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.340
How old are you now ?

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:21.060
18 years of age,
Your Excellency.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.800
How many times does he have
to ask the same question ?

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:28.420
I, too, was once
18 years old.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:29.670
Naturally !

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:33.880
That was 48 years ago.

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:39.460
If you'll excuse me, you meant
58 years ago, didn't you ?

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:46.300
Ah, perhaps that's right.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:50.390
I wouldn't mind either way.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:53.120
That's not a
critical issue.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:05:00.000
Of course it's not a critical issue; the ten years
age difference to an incompetent old admiral.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:02.470
Commodore Musel...

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:11.630
...you have everything that I wish
I had when I was 18 years old.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:13.690
I'm envious of you.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:15.400
Huh ?

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:21.290
When I was 18, I was a
student at a military school...

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:26.370
...but I wasn't a valedictorian or
anything, just an average student.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:29.970
And of course, I wasn't
particularly handsome.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:33.770
I didn't have a
close friend, either.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.950
You have every
one of those.

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.740
I'm envious.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:44.920
But Your Excellency, you're from
a renowned viscount's family.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:47.960
As for myself, I'm a <i>Reichsleiter</i>;
an aristocrat only in name.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:52.820
I was the third child.

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:58.910
Only because both of my elder brothers died in
the war was I able to inherit the viscount lineage.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:07.620
If my brothers had lived, I probably would
have been granted a barony out of pity...

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:11.440
...and been kept in
meaningless service for life.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:19.740
When I see you, Commodore Musel,
you seem bright and shining.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.000
I'm overwhelmed.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:24.440
What's he talking about ?

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.720
He's envious of me ?

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:31.820
Even though he was born of a renowned
lineage and favored by the Kaiser ?

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:37.920
Is it because he's old ?

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.640
Or because he's
lacking talent ?

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:44.660
I suppose I can't
comprehend such feelings.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:48.840
We're moving away
from the front line.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.970
Is that okay with
you, Lord Reinhard ?

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:55.100
Ah, yes.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.800
We'll do as ordered.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.200
Instruct the crew to
prepare to move out.{traveling}

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:09.160
Order acknowledged.

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:16.020
Did something happen between Lord
Reinhard and Vice Admiral Grimmelshausen ?

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:20.620
Thus, the Empire's
Grimmelshausen Fleet...

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:24.980
...headed toward Van-Fleet 4-2
for an unconstructive reason.

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:29.670
But even though the Imperial Fleet was not
aware of it, the satellite already had a "guest."

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:35.230
That is, about 100 days ago, an
Alliance rear-line base was built there.

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:39.130
Why is an Imperial
fleet coming here ?

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:43.740
We chose this location as a rear-line base precisely because it was so far away from the front line.

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:47.720
The Alliance base commander...

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:52.350
...Vice Admiral Cerebrese was renowned
for his rear-line support capabilities.

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:58.940
Despite his brilliance in logistics, he could
not comprehend the Imperial Fleet's intentions.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.720
There was no way
he could have known...

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:06.150
...the absurd reason for which the
fleet was sent to this remote place:

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:08.350
...that the commander of the fleet
was disliked by his Fleet HQ.

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:16.550
I see, the Imperial Fleet considers
this base to be of much importance.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:19.710
After all, they've
sent a whole fleet.

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:27.700
They must be planning to overwhelm us and obliterate this base, then build a permanent base of their own.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:28.950
Is that so ?

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:31.090
That's the only
possibility that makes sense.

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:32.820
Summon Colonel Wahnschaffe.

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:36.020
We're mobilizing the
Rosenritter Regiment ?

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:36.980
Yes.

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:38.270
There's no other way !

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:41.580
Instead of asking meaningless questions,
just call up Colonel Wahnschaffe !

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:42.920
We haven't got
time to waste !

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:54.670
Colonel Wahnschaffe reporting.

00:08:56.690 --> 00:09:00.120
Colonel Otto Frank von Wahnschaffe...

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:03.720
...is the 12th commanding officer
of the Rosenritter Regiment...

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:07.660
...which is comprised of Imperial
refugees and their children.

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:13.590
Though it's not particularly rare, he himself is
said to be from a military family in the Empire.

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:19.150
So you believe the enemy fleet
is aiming for this base ?

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:20.470
Of course.

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:26.370
Anyway, it is a matter of fact that the
enemy fleet has control of the northern sphere.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:28.770
In order for us to discover
their precise intentions...

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:32.470
...I'd like you to send a
reconnaissance group immediately.

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:33.520
Understood, sir.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:44.570
Lt. Colonel Schenkopp.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:07.480
It actually seems to be a fact that an Imperial fleet has occupied the north pole of this satellite.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:08.590
Oh.

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:12.830
So how much did you sell them
out for, Regiment Commander ?

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:14.740
I didn't sell anyone out.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:17.400
He doesn't know
how to take a joke.

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:19.260
We'll send a
reconnaissance unit.

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:22.570
Prepare 6 armored
vehicles and 35 soldiers.

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:24.590
When will we go ?

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:26.280
You don't need to go.

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:28.300
I'll lead the mission and you'll be
in charge during my absence.

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:31.270
I understand.

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:35.530
But I think it'd be wiser not
to take unnecessary actions.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:38.720
They didn't launch an
attack from orbit...

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:41.190
...which means they probably
aren't aware of our presence.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:46.420
Like poking a stick into a bush and finding a
snake or worse, a family of big, poisonous snakes...

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:49.910
...unnecessary actions might
actually trigger their reaction.

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:51.670
You might be right.

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:56.050
But, Lt. Colonel, I don't
need your advice.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:59.010
I apologize for my impudence.

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:12.660
What's your opinion, Captain Linz ?

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:14.120
If we move around needlessly...

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:19.160
...we might be found and invite a
large scale attack from the enemy.

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:22.450
Didn't you warn the
regiment commander, Lt. Colonel ?

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:24.250
Of course I did.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:28.440
It looks like the commander doesn't want to
miss this opportunity to become a Brigadier.

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:30.120
In that case...

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:32.600
...I suppose he's aiming for a special,
two-rank jump to become a Major General ?

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:39.640
In any case, what are the Imperial
Fleet's intentions in landing here ?

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:46.560
I haven't the slightest idea what the stuck-up
nobles of the heaven-favored Galactic Empire...

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:49.340
...sitting pretty above the
clouds have in their minds.

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:53.190
I'm just an aristocrat in
name - that's way beyond me.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:56.800
What should we do, Lt. Colonel ?

00:11:57.590 --> 00:11:58.970
Let's see.

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:02.370
We should eat well, sleep well,
and be strong and well.

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:05.490
The goddess of fate doesn't
like weak and sick men.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:18.890
So you claim there's an Alliance
base south of this satellite's north pole ?

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:20.760
Yes, sir.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:24.120
The results of our analysis
of enemy communications...

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:26.180
...indicate that it's highly plausible.

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:32.670
First, I propose that we send unmanned
reconnaissance planes to investigate the area.

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:43.650
What do you all think of
Commodore Musel's opinion ?

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:49.940
I have a feeling that it is something
we should give serious consideration.

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:57.120
If Commodore Musel's
supposition is correct...

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:03.720
...unnecessary reconnaissance may
instead reveal our position.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:08.120
And if the enemy force is weaker than
we are, then it won't pose any threat...

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:13.300
...even if we just wait and
counterattack after they strike.

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:17.430
In other words,
it's a do-nothing policy.

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:20.400
These men are up to their necks
in corruption and degeneracy.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:27.590
If the presupposed danger is the only reason
for not authorizing a reconnaissance mission...

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:29.910
...I will gladly
volunteer for the task.

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:35.420
Commanders, I ask permission for
activities outside our air-defense zone.

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:44.260
The orders from Fleet
Headquarters are to wait.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:47.760
If we take meaningless actions for an
impatient pursuit of our own interests...

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:54.870
...it might affect the larger outcome of the battle and give an advantage to the enemy.

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:58.600
That's what has us concerned.

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:00.590
But...

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:04.230
Commodore Musel,
there's no need to rush.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:08.460
There's indeed no rush.

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:18.020
Since your elders are in agreement why don't we wait for now and see how the enemy moves ?

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:21.940
But of course, that's if there
indeed is an enemy force.

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:23.330
Please wait, Your Excellency.

00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:26.350
Huh ?

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:31.340
I also believe there's
a need for reconnaissance.

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:39.720
If you'll excuse my impudence...

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:44.100
...you all know that I have inside
information on the Alliance forces.

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:50.980
Speaking from that experience,
I think there's a strong possibility...

00:14:50.980 --> 00:14:56.290
...that the enemy has a supply and
rear-line support base in this area of space.

00:14:57.230 --> 00:15:03.700
As for a place here where they can
build a base, only Van-Fleet 4-2 qualifies.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:13.230
Information on the enemy's position and strength
may prove to be useful in the course of this battle.

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:24.820
But even though Commodore Musel is 
said to be gifted in leading space battles...

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:29.230
...I have more experience
in the area of ground combat.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:35.600
As for the reconnaissance mission,
I would like to have you leave it to me.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:40.020
This guy is trying to steal my
chance to make a name for myself...

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:41.950
...or is there something
else going on ?

00:15:43.510 --> 00:15:45.550
Ah yes, you are right.

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:47.000
That sounds better.

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:54.150
Commodore Musel, I think it's better
to leave this task to Luneberg.

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:55.950
What do you think ?

00:15:56.710 --> 00:16:01.380
After all, Luneberg is an
expert in ground combat.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:05.600
As you please,
Your Excellency.

00:16:08.430 --> 00:16:10.670
It's ridiculous to 
even try and argue.

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:15.670
But this guy, Luneberg...

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:17.980
...he is said to be an
expert in ground combat...

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:20.370
But what is he really ?

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:35.590
Where is Colonel Wahnschaffe ?

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:37.190
He hasn't returned yet.

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:40.010
Damn, what a bother.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:43.670
Hey, Linz,
Blumhart, Der Decken...

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:46.670
...we'll go do some light
after-meal exercise.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:50.670
Um, no, I haven't
finished eating yet.

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:56.720
Since I'm of good upbringing,
I don't eat fast like you, Lt. Colonel....

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:33.690
Hey look, that's the strongest
quartet of the Rosenritter.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:37.590
Lt. Colonel Schenkopp is said to be a
better fighter than the regimental commander.

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:12.400
Is this okay with you ?

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:15.820
Everyone knows how competent
Lt. Colonel Schenkopp is.

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:20.850
As long as he doesn't hold any crazy
thoughts, he could make general someday.

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:22.980
"Crazy thoughts" ?

00:18:24.430 --> 00:18:27.670
Out of 11 Rosenritter commanders...

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:32.270
...two made the jump to general,
three died in the battle...

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:35.100
...and six went back
to the Empire.

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:40.260
The Rosenritter Regiment
always poses that danger.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:48.230
But in the case of Lt. Colonel Schenkopp,
it's said that there's another kind of "danger."

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.960
By which you mean ?

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:53.300
It's a coup d'etat.

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:54.950
It can't be.

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:59.230
He might be just a whiner.

00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:02.760
But he is a highly competent whiner.

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:05.590
There's no doubt he's
a dangerous presence.

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:14.740
But in any case was there a reason for the commander to go on the reconnaissance himself ?

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.670
He might be planning
to return to the Empire.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:20.210
He might have received an
invitation to that effect.

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:25.420
In my case, too, I would take the offer if a
red-haired beauty came to me with dollar bills.

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:29.120
I'm sorry.

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:30.290
It was a bad joke.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:37.270
After our previous commander left the Alliance for the Empire the regiment was almost abolished.

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:39.980
They couldn't have
abolished it, though.

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:45.360
To begin with, the Rosenritter were
founded to be used as propaganda.

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:48.850
If they abolish us, it
would defeat their purpose.

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:51.230
Besides, because the
former commander defected...

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:55.630
...the present members fight even
harder than before to clear their names.

00:19:57.510 --> 00:20:02.850
But in any case, it's a pity that we
must continue to fight and shed blood...

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:07.010
...just to make people acknowledge
our existence, our legitimacy.

00:20:09.530 --> 00:20:12.420
Drei rot, drei rot.

00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:17.430
In my life and death...

00:20:17.430 --> 00:20:25.210
Red is a cursed color.

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:34.480
Blood, Fire, and Scarlet Roses...

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:43.560
Simply color my life.

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:46.740
Drei Rot...

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:50.050
Three red, isn't it ?

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:54.420
The previous regimental
commander used to sing it.

00:20:55.120 --> 00:21:00.470
No one has sung it since he defected -
it's been a long time since I've heard that song.

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:03.640
I like this song.

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:09.130
Especially because my father hates
it when I sing it in front of him.

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:19.100
But where is the present regimental
commander enjoying his picnic ?

00:21:19.100 --> 00:21:22.400
I wouldn't think he lost his way,
but it won't do us any good...

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:25.010
...if he wanders about and gets
discovered by the enemy.

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:28.330
We can't let them find out that
we have a base on this satellite.

00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:32.970
There's no chance we'll win if we have
to go up against a fleet of battleships.

00:21:34.130 --> 00:21:38.410
So it's for the better
if they don't discover us.

00:21:38.410 --> 00:21:43.670
But of course, if there's someone
with a brain among the enemy...

00:21:43.670 --> 00:21:49.400
...and if they start investigating the
whole area, that'll be the end of it.

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.620
What's with him,
that man, Luneberg ?

00:22:01.570 --> 00:22:02.840
What's happened now ?

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:08.370
That bastard, he asked the commanders to
make me subcaptain of the ground troops.

00:22:08.370 --> 00:22:09.890
He's a commodore, too.

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:12.650
Why do I have to serve
under someone of equal rank ?

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:19.120
Commodore Luneberg is 17
years older than you are...

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:21.690
...and he was appointed
a commodore before you were.

00:22:21.690 --> 00:22:24.230
He's also an expert
in ground combat.

00:22:24.230 --> 00:22:26.450
I beg you to
bear with this.

00:22:35.810 --> 00:22:37.550
Say, Kircheis...

00:22:37.550 --> 00:22:38.710
Yes.

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:43.020
As it is, I'm still serving
under a commodore like Luneberg.

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:48.230
Will it be possible for me to seize
control of the Empire like this ?

00:22:48.230 --> 00:22:52.120
What I'm holding inside of
me may not be an ambition.

00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:54.100
It might just
be a delusion.

00:22:57.740 --> 00:22:58.710
Lord Reinhard...

00:23:01.150 --> 00:23:05.370
Lord Reinhard detests the whole
idea of serving under other people.

00:23:06.160 --> 00:23:08.760
He was like that even when we
were still at military school.

00:23:09.910 --> 00:23:14.290
Lord Reinhard, this will be a
good learning experience for you.

00:23:14.290 --> 00:23:19.570
You've passed over many people
to arrive at your present rank.

00:23:19.570 --> 00:23:25.170
If this experience teaches you what
it feels like to be passed over...

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:30.870
...this assignment might not
be too unreasonable after all.

00:23:33.650 --> 00:23:36.920
There you go again with
your worrywart personality.

00:23:36.920 --> 00:23:41.680
If you worry so much all the time,
your nice red hair will soon turn gray.

00:23:42.910 --> 00:23:47.250
I wasn't born with a
worrywart personality, but...

00:23:47.630 --> 00:23:48.660
Of course you weren't.{didn't.}

00:23:48.660 --> 00:23:51.930
If there's an infant with a worrywart
personality, I'd like to see it.

00:23:55.600 --> 00:23:58.000
That wasn't what
I meant, but...

00:23:58.670 --> 00:23:59.660
He can be a
pain sometimes.

00:24:01.620 --> 00:24:06.420
Siegfried Kircheis, ever since he
met the Musels eight years ago...

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:11.230
...and was asked by Annerose to be Reinhard's
friend, has firmly kept that promise in his heart...

00:24:11.230 --> 00:24:14.130
...while fighting all the battles.

00:24:16.100 --> 00:24:20.680
The reason he fights is for this sister and brother, and only for them.

00:24:24.630 --> 00:24:31.520
On March 29th of Space
Year 794, Imperial Year 485...

00:24:31.520 --> 00:24:42.680
...on Van-Fleet 4-2, a small battle that eventually turns out to bear a larger significance was about to begin.

